.TITLE "chown"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Changes the user and group ownership of files and directories. It is a critical tool for __system administration__ and managing file access security.

.DIV "TLDR"
**chown user file**
Changes the owner of a file to the specified user.
> __user__ the new owner | __file__ the target file

**chown user:group file**
Changes both the owner and the group of a file simultaneously.
> __user:group__ new owner and group | __file__ the target file

**chown :group file**
Changes only the group ownership of a file.
> __:group__ the new group | __file__ the target file

**chown -R user folder**
Recursively changes the ownership of a directory and all its contents.
> __-R__ recursive flag | __user__ the new owner | __folder__ target directory

.DIV "SUMMARY"
You typically need __root privileges__ (using __sudo__) to change file ownership. The __user:group__ syntax is the most efficient way to fully reassign a file's security context in a single command.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**cli:chmod** **cli:chgrp** **cli:ls**

